{{also|compétition}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|compétition}}, from {{der|en|LL.|competitio|competītiō, competītiōnem}}, from {{der|en|la|competō}}, from {{m|la|con-}} + {{m|la|petō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌkɒmpəˈtɪʃən/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˌkɑːmpəˈtɪʃən/|a=GenAm}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-competition.ogg|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The action of [[compete|competing]].
#: {{ux|en|The '''competition''' for this job is strong.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=8|passage=The humor of my proposition appealed more strongly to Miss Trevor than I had looked for, and from that time forward she became her old self again;{{...}}. Our table in the dining-room became again the abode of scintillating wit and caustic repartee, Farrar bracing up to his old standard, and the demand for seats in the vicinity rose to an animated '''competition'''.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[contest]] for a prize or award.
#: {{ux|en|The newspaper is featuring a '''competition''' to win a car.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|collectively}} The [[competitor]]s in such a contest.
#: {{ux|en|The new stain remover was ten times more effective than the '''competition'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=6 February 2013|editors=Michio Muramatsu; Frieder Naschold|author=Hideo Otake|chapter=Revising the Interpretation of the Japanese Economy|title=State and Administration in Japan and Germany: A Comparative Perspective on Continuity and Change|page=319|url=https://books.google.co.nz/books?id=lc4fAAAAQBAJ|passage=Japanese retail stores have strove to, and have succeeded in, fulfilling these severe demands, and in doing so, have constantly had to innovate both technologically and institutionally in order to keep up with the '''competition'''.}}

